+#pragma once
+
+#include <string>
+
+/* STEP (ISO 10303) import, bridging OpenCASCADE (STEP read + tessellate)
+   into nanoPRC's own write API (tessellation -> PRC -> PDF). Two
+   implementations exist -- step_import.cpp (real, built only when
+   OpenCASCADE was found at configure time) and step_import_stub.cpp (a
+   stand-in that always fails with a clear message, built otherwise) --
+   selected by demos/viewer/CMakeLists.txt so this header's callers never
+   need to know which one they got.
+
+   SCOPE: converts geometry only (every solid in the file, tessellated,
+   each becoming its own PRC part so the viewer's per-part Scene tree stays
+   useful). Does NOT carry over STEP assembly names/hierarchy (every solid
+   in the file is flattened into one level, named "Solid N"), colors, or
+   PMI/metadata -- nanoPRC's write API has no color/material/style
+   parameters to hand any of that to even if this code extracted it. This
+   is geometry-only import, not a STEP-to-3D-PDF archival tool. */
+
+/* Converts step_path to a new temporary 3D PDF (via OpenCASCADE tessellation
+   + nanoPRC's write API) and writes its path to out_pdf_path. The file is
+   NOT cleaned up automatically -- it needs to outlive this call so the
+   caller can hand it to a fresh viewer process; delete it once that
+   process has loaded it, or just leave it (it's under the system temp
+   directory).
+
+   Returns true on success. Returns false and fills out_error with a
+   human-readable message (safe to show directly in a dialog) on failure,
+   including when this build has no STEP import support at all. */
+bool ImportStepToTempPdf(const char *step_path, std::string &out_pdf_path, std::string &out_error);
+
+/* Whether this build was compiled with STEP import support (OpenCASCADE
+   found at build time) -- lets the caller decide whether to even attempt
+   ImportStepToTempPdf, e.g. to skip the file-picker step and go straight
+   to an explanatory dialog. */
+bool StepImportAvailable();
